+## New during the hackathon (from 2026-10-27)
+
+Everything up to commit `0d3dde1` (2026-10-19) existed before the hackathon: the seven-agent
+pipeline, the sandbox, the verifier, the dashboard, the mock provider, the Meta provider (written to
+the documented contract but never run), defects D1–D5 and the one-shot benchmark. Built during the
+hackathon:
+
+1. **First real-model runs on Muse Spark 1.3**, and the fixes they forced: replies cut off at
+   `max_completion_tokens` are retried with a higher limit, and a probe failed by the runtime
+   (`unhandledRejection`) is no longer scored as evidence against a correct prediction.
+2. **A fair baseline.** Baseline C is an edit → run tests → retry loop with the same call budget as
+   FORGE-0, the way coding agents work today; the benchmark compares all three systems.
+3. **Harder defects.** D6–D9, each designed to defeat a one-shot fix (two causes, a contract tested
+   in another file, a stateful regex, an order-dependent test).
+4. **A real open-source bug.** R1: [`parse`](https://github.com/r1chardj0n3s/parse) issue #162,
+   vendored at the commit before the upstream fix, with the project's own regression test. This
+   also made the **pytest** runner real (JUnit XML parsing, test selection plugin).
+5. **Flaky-test triage.** Re-runs classify every failure as deterministic, intermittent or
+   order-dependent before any hypothesis; the verifier adapts its re-runs to the class.
+6. **GitHub integration.** `forge0-ci` + a workflow template ([integrations/github](integrations/github/README.md)):
+   on a CI failure or a `forge0`-labelled issue, it opens a PR whose description is the evidence,
+   or comments the evidence when no fix survives verification.
+7. **Two Meta models in two roles.** Muse Spark 1.3 forms the hypotheses; the open-weights Muse
+   Spark Open designs experiments and writes repairs. Each call records which model served it.
+8. **Smarter context selection.** Relevant files are ranked (stack trace → files they name → their
+   imports) so a root cause two imports away is not cut by the file cap.
+
