+`forge0-ci` runs an investigation headlessly and reports on GitHub: a verified fix becomes a pull
+request whose description is the evidence (explanations considered, experiments, verification,
+diff); otherwise the evidence goes into an issue comment. It never opens a PR for an unverified
+patch. Setup: [integrations/github/README.md](integrations/github/README.md).
 
-Each claimed patch is applied to a fresh copy together with **hidden tests** neither system has
-seen. Results land in `benchmarks/results/` (JSON + HTML) and on the **Evaluation** page.
-Methodology, metric definitions and the current (mock-only) numbers are in
-[docs/EVALUATION.md](docs/EVALUATION.md). Those numbers reflect scripted fixtures, not model
-capability.
+```bash
+forge0-ci --repo . --issue-body-file issue.md --comment-issue 42 --open-pr --base main
+forge0-ci --repo . --dry-run          # investigate for real, print the git/gh commands instead
+```
 
